{"name":"Rhythm","hex":"#767194","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rhythm","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The variation of strong and weak elements (such as duration, accent) of sounds, notably in speech or music, over time; a beat or meter.","A specifically defined pattern of such variation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To impart a (particular) rhythm to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhythm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rhythm","blocks":[{"text":"Rhythm generally means a \"movement marked by the regulated succession of strong and weak elements, or of opposite or different conditions\". This general meaning of regular recurrence or pattern in time can apply to a wide variety of cyclical natural phenomena having a periodicity or frequency of anything from microseconds to several seconds ; to several minutes or hours, or, at the most extreme, even over many years."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhythm"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Traditional_indonesian_instruments02.jpg/500px-Traditional_indonesian_instruments02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Traditional_indonesian_instruments02.jpg/1280px-Traditional_indonesian_instruments02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Traditional_indonesian_instruments02.jpg/500px-Traditional_indonesian_instruments02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Percussion instruments have clearly defined sounds that aid the creation and perception of complex rhythms.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATraditional_indonesian_instruments02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Compound_triple_drum_pattern.png/500px-Compound_triple_drum_pattern.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Compound_triple_drum_pattern.png/500px-Compound_triple_drum_pattern.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Compound triple drum pattern: divides three beats into three; contains repetition on three levels ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACompound_triple_drum_pattern.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Claves-detail.gif/500px-Claves-detail.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Claves-detail.gif/500px-Claves-detail.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Notation of a clave rhythm pattern: Each cell of the grid corresponds to a fixed duration of time with a resolution fine enough to capture the timing of the pattern, which may be counted as two bars of four beats in divisive (metrical or symmetrical) rhythm, each beat divided into two cells. The first bar of the pattern may also usefully be counted additively (in measured or asymmetrical rhythm) as 3 + 3 + 2.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClaves-detail.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Phenakistoscope_3g07690d.gif/500px-Phenakistoscope_3g07690d.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Phenakistoscope_3g07690d.gif/500px-Phenakistoscope_3g07690d.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An early moving picture demonstrates the waltz, a dance in triple metre.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhenakistoscope_3g07690d.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Bach%2C_Sinfonia_in_F_minor_BWV_795%2C_mm._1-3a_composite_rhythm.png/500px-Bach%2C_Sinfonia_in_F_minor_BWV_795%2C_mm._1-3a_composite_rhythm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Bach%2C_Sinfonia_in_F_minor_BWV_795%2C_mm._1-3a_composite_rhythm.png/1280px-Bach%2C_Sinfonia_in_F_minor_BWV_795%2C_mm._1-3a_composite_rhythm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Bach%2C_Sinfonia_in_F_minor_BWV_795%2C_mm._1-3a_composite_rhythm.png/500px-Bach%2C_Sinfonia_in_F_minor_BWV_795%2C_mm._1-3a_composite_rhythm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bach's Sinfonia in F minor BWV 795, mm. 1–3\nOriginal\nWith composite","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABach%2C_Sinfonia_in_F_minor_BWV_795%2C_mm._1-3a_composite_rhythm.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Diffa_Niger_Griot_DSC_0177.jpg/500px-Diffa_Niger_Griot_DSC_0177.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Diffa_Niger_Griot_DSC_0177.jpg/500px-Diffa_Niger_Griot_DSC_0177.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Griot performs at Diffa, Niger, West Africa. The Griot is playing a Ngoni or Xalam.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiffa_Niger_Griot_DSC_0177.jpg"}],"sounds":{"rhythm":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-rhythm.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/59/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-rhythm.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-rhythm.wav.mp3